      "content": "You're right to look beyond Europe, as other cultures were making significant strides during that time. Islamic scholars preserved and expanded upon Greek knowledge, making huge advances in mathematics, medicine, and astronomy. Similarly, ancient and medieval Chinese civilization developed sophisticated bureaucratic systems, advanced technologies like gunpowder, and complex legal frameworks long before much of Europe caught up. These non-European contributions were vital to the global progression of knowledge.",
